Fillets and chamfers: the pieces of an edge's analytic blend over a hole
or cut-out of its face, cut there by the faces beyond (0055, 0057, 0071),
are one face with the hole cut out (mitcad#121). Before, the blend was a
face per piece, with edges between them across the blend.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKPart: of an edge's pieces in order along
  the spine, a run from a piece through pieces whose contact on one side
  lies on other faces (cut there by the faces beyond) to a piece whose
  contacts lie on the faces of the first again, all on one surface (the
  same analytic surface and parametrization, ChFi3d_SameAnalyticSurface),
  gets one surface index in the data structure. Pieces split where a
  contact passes from one face to another keep their own faces.
- ChFi3d_FilDS: a piece on the surface of the one before it adds no
  solid-surface interference and gets no section between them; the rest
  of a section shared in part (0071) is still its edge with the face
  beyond.
